1
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:10,040
Thank you.
谢谢。

2
00:00:11,790 --> 00:00:13,123
All right, friends.
好的，朋友们。

3
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:14,630
You know how we do.
大家知道我们的口号。

4
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:17,390
Money out of politics.
让金钱退出政治。

5
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:19,090
Money in your pocket.
让人民的口袋充实起来。

6
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:21,390
Medicare for All.
全民医疗保险。

7
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:23,490
Michigan, we did it.
密歇根，我们做到了！

8
00:00:32,910 --> 00:00:43,290
My name is Abdulrahman Mohamed El-Sayed.
我叫阿卜杜勒拉赫曼·穆罕默德·埃尔-赛义德。

9
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:52,527
And I am so proud and honored to stand here as your senator elect from the great state of Michigan.
能作为伟大密歇根州的候任参议员站在这里，我无比自豪、无比荣幸。

10
00:00:54,880 --> 00:01:03,980
Up until right about now, you might have noticed I always say inshallah or God willing whenever the outcome of this race was mentioned.
你们可能注意到，此前每次提到选举结果，我都会说“inshallah”，意思是“如果真主愿意”。

11
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:12,695
But today, tonight, we can turn that inshallah into an alhamdulillah.
但今天，今晚，我们可以把“如果真主愿意”，变成“alhamdulillah”。

12
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:32,880
For the right-wing ops, that just means praise be to God.
给那些右翼操盘手解释一下：这句话只是“赞颂真主”的意思。

13
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:43,080
This movement for money out of politics, money in your pocket, and Medicare for All, I just want to thank you everybody who knocked the door,
对于这场要求金钱退出政治、让人民口袋充实、实行全民医保的运动，我要感谢每一个敲门的人，

14
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:53,280
Made a call, sent a dollar, posted a story, and most importantly, gave us your stake in democracy.
打电话、捐一美元、发一条动态，以及最重要的，把自己的民主权利托付给我们的人。

15
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:59,720
You took a chance on the unlikeliest of candidates.
你们愿意相信一个最不被看好的候选人。

16
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:01,020
So thank you.
所以，谢谢你们。

17
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:04,720
This is all yours.
这一切都属于你们。

18
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:16,360
Michigan, I cannot wait to serve you with the same big-heartedness, open-mindedness, grit, and earnestness that you've shown me.
密歇根，我迫不及待要以你们展现给我的宽厚、开放、坚韧和真诚，为你们服务。

19
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:22,780
You welcomed me to your homes, your churches, your synagogues, your VFW and union halls.
你们欢迎我走进家中、教堂、犹太会堂、退伍军人会馆和工会大厅。

20
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:27,500
You shared moments of frustration and sadness and vulnerability with me.
与我分享挫折、悲伤和脆弱的时刻。

21
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:31,580
You gave me grace and strength in my lowest moments.
在我最低落的时候，给予我宽容和力量。

22
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:35,580
And the hope and inspiration that powered my best.
也给予我希望与鼓舞，让我拿出最好的自己。

23
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:38,146
I love you back.
我也爱你们。

24
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:42,090
And I hope that I can bring it all with me.
我希望把这一切都带在身边。

25
00:02:43,210 --> 00:02:46,730
I hope I can bring it all with me to Washington in your service.
把这一切带到华盛顿，为你们服务。

26
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:56,020
Thank you for your trust and your belief and your kindness.
感谢你们的信任、信念和善意。

27
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:04,120
I'm going to take it all with me and I hope to bring back the kind of leadership that more than earns it.
我会带着这一切，也希望带回一种真正配得上它们的领导方式。

28
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:09,482
The last month has brought the stakes of this election into sharp relief.
过去一个月，让这场选举的利害关系变得格外清楚。

29
00:03:09,482 --> 00:03:16,560
Ours, this beautiful movement was built over the past year and a half campaigning across Michigan's biggest cities and its smallest towns.
我们的这场美丽运动，是过去一年半走遍密歇根大城市、小城镇建立起来的。

30
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,880
We spoke of a brighter, a bigger, more hopeful Michigan.
我们谈论一个更光明、更宽广、更有希望的密歇根。

31
00:03:20,792 --> 00:03:28,040
Theirs, an astroturfed corporate-funded advertising campaign built to deceive and distract.
他们的，则是一场由企业出钱、伪装成民间行动，意在欺骗和转移视线的广告攻势。

32
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:43,350
Rather than try to unite us to contend with the crisis of gas or groceries, the opposition decided to try to divide us.
对手没有团结大家应对油价、食品价格危机，而是选择分裂我们。

33
00:03:43,970 --> 00:03:50,130
At first, they pointed to my name and my faith as if to say, you know, he's a little different.
起初，他们拿我的名字、我的信仰说事，仿佛在说：“他和我们有点不一样。”

34
00:03:51,230 --> 00:03:55,030
And when it didn't work, they tried to guilt me by association.
没有奏效，他们就试图用牵连的方式给我定罪。

35
00:03:55,730 --> 00:04:01,270
And when that didn't work, they went all in on one of the ugliest campaigns we've seen in our lifetimes.
还不奏效，他们便全力发动我们一生中所见最丑恶的竞选攻势之一。

36
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:12,840
They might have been pointing to my name and my faith, but we all know that my name and my faith aren't the reason you can't afford your gas.
他们针对的也许是我的名字和信仰，但大家都知道，那并不是你加不起油的原因。

37
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,780
Not the reason you can't afford your groceries.
不是你买不起食品的原因。

38
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,820
Not the reason you can't see a doctor.
不是你看不起医生的原因。

39
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:26,530
Now, as I was campaigning, some of you would come up and ask me, how come you don't hit back?
竞选期间，有些人问我：你为什么不还击？

40
00:04:27,490 --> 00:04:30,130
How come you don't call them racist or hateful?
为什么不说他们种族歧视、充满仇恨？

41
00:04:31,650 --> 00:04:33,930
Because here's the thing, I didn't run for myself.
因为，我不是为了自己才参选。

42
00:04:34,730 --> 00:04:37,830
And in truth, they weren't targeting me.
事实上，他们针对的也不是我。

43
00:04:39,590 --> 00:04:42,384
They weren't just attacking me.
他们不只是在攻击我。

44
00:04:42,384 --> 00:04:45,350
They were targeting and attacking you.
他们针对、攻击的，是你们。

45
00:04:46,410 --> 00:04:50,630
They were targeting and attacking the very idea of America.
是美国这个理念本身。

46
00:04:52,150 --> 00:04:59,690
See, they hate the idea of an America big enough for anyone who looks a little different or prays a little different or whose family comes from a different part of the World.
他们不愿看到一个足够宽广的美国，能够容纳长相不同、祈祷方式不同，或家庭来自世界其他地方的人。

47
00:05:01,310 --> 00:05:07,270
That includes me, but it also includes anyone and everyone who doesn't look like them, pray like them,
这当然包括我，也包括所有长得不像他们、祈祷方式不像他们，

48
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:09,490
Love like them, or isn't rich like them.
爱得不像他们，或者没有他们富有的人。

49
00:05:10,270 --> 00:05:12,590
So they turned this race into a simple choice.
所以，他们让这场选举变成一个简单的选择。

50
00:05:13,510 --> 00:05:16,010
They want an America that is too small for some of us.
他们想要一个狭小到容不下我们某些人的美国。

51
00:05:16,130 --> 00:05:19,570
We know that America is big enough for all of us.
而我们知道，美国足够宽广，能容下我们所有人。

52
00:05:21,094 --> 00:05:22,253
Big enough.
足够宽广。

53
00:05:22,253 --> 00:05:26,650
We're big enough to take on the crises that we face.
也足够强大，能够应对面前的危机。

54
00:05:27,294 --> 00:05:30,050
Day by day, Trump's insults became uglier and coarser.
一天天地，特朗普的侮辱变得更恶毒、更粗鄙。

55
00:05:30,430 --> 00:05:37,090
But I got to spend those days with you, learning about your struggles, your hopes, and the things that inspire you.
但我却能把那些日子花在和你们相处，了解你们的挣扎、希望，以及给你们力量的事物。

56
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:46,730
A mom of two kids with a genetic lung disease in East Jordan, fighting the system to make sure her kids don't lose the meds that they rely on to stay alive.
东乔丹的一位母亲，两个孩子都患遗传性肺病；她与体制抗争，确保孩子不会失去赖以维生的药物。

57
00:05:46,730 --> 00:05:50,890
Her hope, that they don't have to struggle with health insurance like she has.
她希望，孩子不必像她一样，为医疗保险苦苦挣扎。

58
00:05:51,370 --> 00:05:57,010
A grandma on the East Side fighting to make sure that the violence that took her son doesn't take her grandson, Too.
东区的一位祖母，努力不让夺走儿子生命的暴力，再夺走她的孙子，再一次发生。

59
00:05:57,750 --> 00:06:01,470
Her hope, an America where boys get to grow up.
她希望，在美国，男孩子们都能平安长大。

60
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:11,510
I met Josh, the UAW auto worker fighting the corporate bosses who hadn't raised their wages in two decades despite billions in profit.
我遇见了汽车工人乔希，一位汽车工人工会会员；公司利润数十亿，却二十年不涨工资，他正与这些企业老板抗争。

61
00:06:11,510 --> 00:06:13,170
And they won that fight.
而他们赢了。

62
00:06:13,770 --> 00:06:18,950
His hope: an America where every single worker gets the right to a union.
他希望，在美国，每一个工人都有加入工会的权利。

63
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:31,340
I met a small business owner fighting to make sure that a another heart attack doesn't take food off the table for his 30 employees or their families.
一位小企业主，努力确保即使自己再次心脏病发作，也不会让三十名员工及其家人失去生计。

64
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:36,460
His hope that his workers don't have to worry about how they'll feed their families.
他希望，员工不必担心如何养活家人。

65
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,160
See, I didn't get into this to defend myself.
我投身政治，并不是为了保护我自己。

66
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:43,900
No, I got into it because their fights are my fight and their hopes are all of our hopes.
而是因为，他们的奋斗就是我的奋斗，他们的希望就是我们共同的希望。

67
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:46,000
We don't do this work for ourselves.
我们做这些工作，不是为了自己。

68
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:55,400
We do this work for each other to defend us all from another generation's youth, treasure, and opportunity squandered at the altar of endless war.
而是为了彼此，保护所有人，不让又一代人的青春、财富和机会，被献祭给无尽的战争。

69
00:06:56,620 --> 00:07:01,340
To defend us all from corporate oligarchs who bought and sold our government to rig the system against us.
保护我们，不受买卖政府、操纵体制的企业寡头侵害。

70
00:07:01,620 --> 00:07:08,000
To defend us all from a healthcare system more interested in monetizing our illness than healing our bodies and minds.
保护我们，不受那种更关心靠疾病赚钱、而非治愈身心的医疗体制侵害。

71
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:15,140
To defend us all from air too putrid to breathe and water too putrid to drink.
保护我们，免于呼吸恶臭的空气、饮用污浊的水。

72
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:20,140
To defend us all from losing our voting or our reproductive or our human rights.
保护我们的投票权、生育自主权和人权，不被夺走。

73
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:30,100
See, I ran to defend us all from politicians who want to divide us rather than movements that work to dignify us.
我参选，是为了保护大家，不受制造分裂的政客伤害，而是建立让我们有尊严的运动。

74
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:35,485
Across our primary and general election campaigns, they spent over Get this.
初选加上大选，他们花了超过——听好了，

75
00:07:35,485 --> 00:07:38,060
$350 million trying to beat us.
三亿五千万美元，试图击败我们。

76
00:07:40,830 --> 00:07:42,910
That is a record here in Michigan.
这在密歇根创下了纪录。

77
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:48,170
$70 million alone in the primary funded by all the same cats who funded the general election.
光初选就七千万美元，出钱的还是大选中的同一批人。

78
00:07:48,850 --> 00:07:51,090
And that's a record anywhere in this country.
这在全国任何地方，都是纪录。

79
00:07:53,190 --> 00:07:57,990
But y'all, Michigan, we built something bigger than a bank account.
但是密歇根，我们建立的，比一个银行账户更强大。

80
00:07:58,790 --> 00:08:00,450
We built a movement.
我们建立了一场运动。

81
00:08:01,050 --> 00:08:04,430
Government of the people, by the people, and for the people.
一个民有、民治、民享的政府。

82
00:08:05,070 --> 00:08:10,307
We showed that in a battle between the money and the many, that the many really can win.
我们证明，在金钱与广大民众的较量中，广大民众确实能赢。

83
00:08:10,307 --> 00:08:22,550
And so to all the kids who watched this last month, to all the parents who struggled to explain why the president openly mocked someone for their name or how they pray,
所有观看了过去一个月的孩子们，以及那些苦于解释总统为什么公开嘲弄别人的名字和祈祷方式的父母们，

84
00:08:22,890 --> 00:08:26,270
Let them know tomorrow that the bad guys lost.
明天，请告诉他们：坏人输了。

85
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:40,480
Let them know I want you to let them know.
告诉他们，我希望你们告诉他们。

86
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:45,880
Let them know that we together, fighting for something bigger, we won.
我们团结起来，为更大的目标而奋斗，我们赢了。

87
00:08:48,510 --> 00:08:51,370
So Mike, enjoy your retirement.
所以迈克，享受你的退休生活吧。

88
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:56,800
I know you got a house in Florida and two yachts.
我知道，你在佛罗里达有房，还有两艘游艇。

89
00:08:58,370 --> 00:09:02,370
See, you chose hate and Michigan chose hope.
你选择了仇恨，密歇根选择了希望。

90
00:09:04,966 --> 00:09:08,887
May we never have to see the likes of you in this state again.
愿我们再也不用在这个州见到你这样的人。

91
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:28,030
JD Habibi there is this delicious irony in the fact that you're constitutionally obligated to swear me in in January.
J.D.，亲爱的，有件事讽刺得令人痛快：按照宪法，一月你必须主持我的就职宣誓。

92
00:09:36,010 --> 00:09:37,010
So you know what that means?
知道这意味着什么吗？

93
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:41,342
Wolverine won, Buckeyes zero.
密歇根狼獾队一分，俄亥俄州立七叶树队零分。

94
00:09:42,301 --> 00:09:52,130
Donald, look, I know you you struggled with my name.
唐纳德，我知道，你一直念不好我的名字。

95
00:09:53,090 --> 00:09:56,790
So after JD swears me in in January, you could just go on and call me senator.
所以一月，J.D.主持我的宣誓之后，你就直接叫我“参议员”好了。

96
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:07,820
To the super PACs and special interests who tried to beat us, we are coming for your system of politics.
那些试图击败我们的超级政治行动委员会和特殊利益集团：我们将挑战你们这套政治制度。

97
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:15,740
To AIPAC, who spent $42 million against us, thank you for giving me the opportunity to beat you twice.
还有花了四千二百万美元反对我们的美以公共事务委员会：谢谢你们给我两次击败你们的机会。

98
00:10:17,586 --> 00:10:21,400
I do want to say something here.
在这里，我确实想说几句话。

99
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:33,560
See, they try to call you hateful if you believe that Palestinian kids should get to grow up in the land of their forefathers without being murdered by our tax dollars.
如果你相信巴勒斯坦的孩子应该在祖辈的土地上长大，而不是被我们的税款资助的武器杀害，他们就试图说你充满仇恨。

100
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:41,380
If you believe in equal rights, to peace, dignity, and self-determination, that's not hate, it's love.
如果你相信平等的权利、和平、尊严和自决，那不是仇恨，而是爱。

101
00:10:42,562 --> 00:10:50,600
Michiganders, we want our taxes spent here, for schools here and health care here and infrastructure here.
密歇根人民，我们希望税款花在这里，建设这里的学校、医疗和基础设施。

102
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:54,760
We don't want our money sent to do apartheid or genocide or war.
我们不希望自己的钱被拿去支持种族隔离、种族灭绝或战争。

103
00:10:55,662 --> 00:11:05,300
Michiganders believe in Michigan, and I believe in Michiganders, and I am so honored that Michiganders believed in me.
密歇根人相信密歇根，我也相信密歇根人；能获得你们的信任，是我的荣幸。

104
00:11:05,354 --> 00:11:08,180
See, you you took a bet on the least likely of candidates.
你们相信了一个最不被看好的候选人。

105
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:09,520
I'm not a politician.
我不是职业政客。

106
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:11,660
I'm a doctor with an 11 letter first name.
我是一个名字有十一个字母的医生。

107
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:18,580
They told us when I started this campaign, there was no way to beat the money.
刚开始竞选时，他们告诉我们：绝不可能战胜金钱。

108
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:24,500
They told us that someone with my name and my story, a Muslim, was unelectable.
他们说，像我这样有着这个名字、这段经历的穆斯林，不可能当选。

109
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:29,260
Let alone in a statewide Senate race in Michigan.
更不可能在密歇根的全州参议员选举中当选。

110
00:11:30,140 --> 00:11:37,760
They told us that old-fashioned politics was dead, that traveling the state to have real conversations with real people in real places was a fool's errand.
他们说，老式政治已经死了；走遍全州，在真实的地方与真实的人真诚交谈，是傻子的差事。

111
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:43,220
They told us that the establishment was too strong, that DC was going to dictate who won and who lost,
他们说，建制势力太强大，华盛顿会决定谁输谁赢，

112
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:46,000
That Washington and its special interests didn't want us.
华盛顿和特殊利益集团不想要我们。

113
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:51,020
They told us that when all the votes had been counted on August 4th and then again on November 3rd,
他们说，八月四日、再到十一月三日，当全部选票开出时，

114
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:53,640
It would have been time and money and energy wasted.
我们投入的时间、金钱、精力，都将白费。

115
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:54,980
Guess what?
猜怎么着？

116
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:56,680
It's November 3rd.
今天就是十一月三日。

117
00:11:58,540 --> 00:11:59,960
And the votes have been counted.
选票已经开出来了。

118
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:02,977
And guess what we just showed them?
猜猜我们刚刚证明了什么？

119
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:07,120
That a movement of the people, by the people, and for the people will ultimately win.
一场民有、民治、民享的运动，最终会赢。

120
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:09,700
Michigan understands the solidarity.
密歇根懂得团结。

121
00:12:10,898 --> 00:12:14,740
It is the people who decide who we send to Washington, and what Washington will do.
决定把谁送往华盛顿、决定华盛顿做什么的，是人民。

122
00:12:14,740 --> 00:12:19,160
We decide, not the big money or their stooges.
是我们决定，不是大金主或他们的傀儡。

123
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:20,920
The people of Michigan will be heard.
密歇根人民的声音，一定会被听见。

124
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:31,420
We showed that we together we can defeat a record $70 million outside spending and 11 to 1 money disadvantage in a primary election,
我们证明，团结起来，就能在初选中战胜创纪录的七千万美元外部支出，以及十一比一的资金劣势，

125
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:34,900
That we can defeat a quarter of a billion dollars in a general election.
能在大选中战胜两亿五千万美元。

126
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:43,060
We can defeat the cynicism of a politics that preys on our earnestness, undersells our intelligence, and exploits our disagreements.
能击败那种利用我们的真诚、低估我们的智慧、挑拨我们的分歧的犬儒政治。

127
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:46,080
Tonight, Michigan, we beat a machine.
今晚，密歇根，我们击败了一部政治机器。

128
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:55,160
And we proved once again just how big America really is.
再次证明，美国的胸襟究竟有多宽广。

129
00:12:56,440 --> 00:13:10,312
Because where else but in America can a doctor named Abdul El-Sayed, a child of immigrants raised by his father and his Daughter of the American Revolution stepmother,
除了美国，还有哪里能让一个名叫阿卜杜勒·埃尔-赛义德的医生、移民之子，由父亲和一位美国革命先辈后裔的继母抚养长大，

130
00:13:10,312 --> 00:13:11,440
Get elected senator from America's greatest state?
最终成为美国最伟大州的参议员？

131
00:13:15,350 --> 00:13:19,250
They tried to confuse you, so let me just set the record straight.
他们试图迷惑你们，那我就把话说清楚。

132
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:21,150
I love America.
我爱美国。

133
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:26,160
I know exactly what America gave to me.
我清楚地知道，美国给了我什么。

134
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:29,920
I saw it up close on trips to my family's native Egypt.
去家人故乡埃及时，我就近距离看到了这些。

135
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:33,960
In a 15-hour journey, I crossed 10 years difference in life expectancy.
十五小时的旅程，跨越的是十年的预期寿命差距。

136
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:35,880
I didn't have to go 15 hours.
其实，我不必走十五小时。

137
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:40,820
I could go 15 minutes to Detroit or Pontiac and cross that same difference.
只要十五分钟，到底特律或庞蒂亚克，我就会跨越同样的差距。

138
00:13:41,899 --> 00:13:43,080
It's why I became a doctor.
所以，我成为了一名医生。

139
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:49,140
America vaccinated me against diseases that killed an aunt and uncle I never got to meet.
美国让我接种疫苗，免于那些夺走我未曾谋面的姑姨和叔伯生命的疾病。

140
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:51,320
It gave me incredible public schools.
它给了我出色的公立学校。

141
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:53,580
It gave me a public university education.
给了我公立大学教育。

142
00:13:53,920 --> 00:13:55,840
It paid my medical education through the NIH.
通过美国国立卫生研究院，资助我接受医学教育。

143
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:57,880
I love America.
我爱美国。

144
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:06,640
But I love America enough to ask her to be America for all her kids.
正因为深爱，我要求她成为属于所有孩子的美国。

145
00:14:08,650 --> 00:14:15,490
See, America is not just a flag, not just our red, white, and blue.
美国不只是一面旗帜，不只是红、白、蓝三种颜色。

146
00:14:15,490 --> 00:14:19,390
It's not a few patriotic songs that we sing or even a landmass we call home.
不只是我们唱的几首爱国歌曲，甚至不只是一片称作家园的土地。

147
00:14:19,850 --> 00:14:25,690
America is about these truths that we hold that all people are created equal.
美国在于我们坚信的真理：人人生而平等。

148
00:14:26,330 --> 00:14:30,210
And the inalienable rights we still struggle to guarantee.
在于我们仍努力保障的那些不可剥夺的权利。

149
00:14:32,630 --> 00:14:35,570
Life, liberty, the pursuit of happiness.
生命、自由，以及追求幸福。

150
00:14:36,670 --> 00:14:44,110
The best of America lives in the audacity of daring a contradiction, a more perfect union.
美国最美好之处，是敢于追求那个看似矛盾的目标：一个更加完善的联邦。

151
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:49,750
That despite the fact that you can't be more than perfect, we embrace the work of perfecting.
即使“完美”似乎无法再进步，我们仍选择不断完善。

152
00:14:50,410 --> 00:14:56,970
America's greatness lives in the moments when free people come together to expand that field of freedom.
美国的伟大，存在于自由的人们团结起来、拓展自由边界的时刻。

153
00:14:58,330 --> 00:15:04,650
America's greatness is the fight to erase the long-standing consequences of slavery and Jim Crow and segregation.
在于努力消除奴隶制、吉姆·克劳法与种族隔离留下的长期伤害。

154
00:15:06,310 --> 00:15:12,390
America's greatness is the fight to embrace all of her people regardless how they pray or if they pray,
在于拥抱每一个人，无论怎样祈祷、是否祈祷，

155
00:15:12,390 --> 00:15:14,390
Who they love, or how they identify.
无论爱谁，或如何认同自己。

156
00:15:15,030 --> 00:15:20,310
America's greatness is in in the union struggle on a shop floor to push off the yoke of greed.
在于车间里工会工人的抗争，挣脱贪婪的枷锁。

157
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:26,370
America's greatness is the fight to guarantee all of us the healthcare we need if we get sick.
在于保障每一个人生病时，都能得到所需的医疗。

158
00:15:27,790 --> 00:15:31,030
Our greatness is the fight for clean air, clean water, and a good home.
在于争取清洁空气、干净饮水和安稳的家。

159
00:15:32,130 --> 00:15:36,830
Our greatness is the fight for equal pay, for equal work, and full freedom of our bodies.
在于争取同工同酬，以及对自己身体的完整自主权。

160
00:15:38,710 --> 00:15:46,210
America's greatness is in the belief a new American still has in the hope that America has always represented.
在于每一位新美国人，仍然相信美国始终代表的那份希望。

161
00:15:47,870 --> 00:15:51,450
America's greatness isn't about ignoring our flaws.
美国的伟大，不在于忽视我们的缺陷。

162
00:15:52,010 --> 00:15:54,890
It's the courage that we have to correct them.
而在于有勇气纠正它们。

163
00:15:56,550 --> 00:15:58,870
Michigan, it just shouldn't be this hard.
密歇根，生活真的不该这么难。

164
00:16:01,450 --> 00:16:04,310
Shouldn't be this hard to buy a second bag of groceries or fill your tank.
不该连多买一袋食品、加满油箱都这么难。

165
00:16:05,110 --> 00:16:06,490
Shouldn't be this hard to afford a home.
不该连买得起房子都这么难。

166
00:16:06,490 --> 00:16:09,930
It shouldn't be this hard to see a doctor in the richest, most powerful country in the world.
在世界上最富有、最强大的国家，看医生不该这么难。

167
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:17,550
It shouldn't be this hard to pay your taxes and know that money is going to be spent on you and your kids instead of dropping bombs on somebody else and their Kids.
纳税后能确信，这钱将用来照顾自己和孩子，而不是轰炸别人的孩子，这不该这么难。

168
00:16:17,926 --> 00:16:20,290
It shouldn't be this hard.
真的不该这么难。

169
00:16:21,910 --> 00:16:23,850
We don't need to be great again.
我们不需要“再次伟大”。

170
00:16:24,770 --> 00:16:28,630
We need to embrace that thing about us that has always made us great.
我们需要拥抱那种一直让我们伟大的品质。

171
00:16:29,870 --> 00:16:32,410
The will to be more perfect.
那就是不断追求更加完善的意志。

172
00:16:33,470 --> 00:16:41,430
And right now that means taking on the corporations and the billionaires, special interests who've rigged the system against us for too long.
而现在，这意味着挑战那些长期操纵体制、侵害我们利益的公司、亿万富翁和特殊利益集团。

173
00:16:43,330 --> 00:16:50,666
Now before I close, I've got some thank yous I've got to get through.
结束之前，我还必须说一些感谢的话。

174
00:17:12,002 --> 00:17:14,160
Sarah, thank you.
萨拉，谢谢你。

175
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:16,560
Thank you for everything.
谢谢你所做的一切。

176
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:21,060
There is no doing this without you and I wouldn't want to do it with anyone else.
没有你，就没有这一切；而我也不愿与任何其他人一起走这段路。

177
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:25,100
I love you and I'm so grateful for you.
我爱你，也深深感激你。

178
00:17:26,702 --> 00:17:30,640
Emmalee and Serene have been my inspiration the entire time.
埃玛莉和瑟琳，一直是我的灵感与动力。

179
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:34,500
I hope someday that they get to read about this in the history books.
希望有一天，她们能在历史书上读到这一切。

180
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:38,940
To understand just how big a part of it they really were.
明白自己其实在其中扮演了多么重要的角色。

181
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:46,180
To my parents and my parents in love, my grandparents, my siblings, my extended family, I can never really repay all that you've poured into me.
感谢父母、岳父母、祖父母、兄弟姐妹和所有家人；你们给予我的，我永远无法完全报答。

182
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:49,800
Thank you always for having my back even if you'd rather I was a surgeon.
谢谢你们一直支持我，尽管你们也许更希望我成为一名外科医生。

183
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:54,679
To my incredible campaign team, Y'all we did it.
我出色的竞选团队，各位，我们做到了。

184
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:05,180
I asked you to lift me up and hold me down and you did both with grace, humility,
我请你们托举我，也让我脚踏实地；你们以宽厚、谦逊，

185
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:06,660
Kindness, and efficiency.
善意和高效，做到了这两件事。

186
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:10,500
No one else I'd rather ride with, best team in American politics.
我最愿意与你们同行，你们是美国政界最好的团队。

187
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:17,940
To all the incredible endorsers who entrusted me with your name, who took time out of your schedule to come campaign with us.
感谢所有出色的支持者，把自己的声誉托付给我，抽出时间来与我们共同竞选。

188
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:21,400
To the Michigan Dems who threw this event for us tonight.
感谢密歇根州民主党，为我们组织今晚的活动。

189
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:27,648
Our chair, Curtis Hertel, who has had our back through thick and thin.
感谢党主席柯蒂斯·赫特尔，无论顺境逆境都支持我们。

190
00:18:28,103 --> 00:18:32,880
To the all the council people and mayors, all the commissioners and county leaders, state reps and state senators,
感谢所有市议员、市长、委员、县级领导、州众议员与州参议员，

191
00:18:33,003 --> 00:18:36,400
Congress people, and US senators, thank you for standing with us.
国会议员和美国参议员，谢谢你们与我们站在一起。

192
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:41,640
And a special thank you to our sisters and brothers in labor.
也特别感谢劳工界的兄弟姐妹。

193
00:18:45,610 --> 00:18:50,640
Your support as a second-generation union member has meant more than you can imagine.
作为第二代工会会员，你们的支持对我意义之大，超乎想象。

194
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:54,300
I cannot wait to stand with you in the fight for Michigan's working people.
我迫不及待要与你们一起，为密歇根的劳动人民奋斗。

195
00:18:55,160 --> 00:19:01,440
To all the community outreach organizations that came through for us in the final stretch, I cannot imagine doing this without you.
感谢所有在最后阶段帮助我们的社区组织；没有你们，这一切难以想象。

196
00:19:01,540 --> 00:19:02,460
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

197
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:08,220
And to all of us here, this fight is not yet over.
在场的每一个人，这场斗争还没有结束。

198
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:14,440
The day I jumped into this race, I promised you that I'd put in the work, fight the fights on your behalf.
参选第一天，我就承诺，为你们努力工作、为你们打该打的仗。

199
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:18,780
I asked you for your time, your energy, your support over the last 19 months.
过去十九个月，我向你们请求时间、精力和支持。

200
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:23,560
Now I'm asking you to support us for the next 6 years.
现在，我请求你们，在接下来的六年继续支持我们。

201
00:19:25,470 --> 00:19:28,830
This work is bigger than one senator.
这项工作，比任何一位参议员都更宏大。

202
00:19:29,530 --> 00:19:32,130
It's about changing the face of our politics.
它关乎改变我们的政治面貌。

203
00:19:32,950 --> 00:19:35,610
So please, do not send me to DC all by myself.
所以，请不要把我一个人送到华盛顿。

204
00:19:36,490 --> 00:19:38,150
All right, I need you all to come with me.
我需要你们所有人，和我一起去。

205
00:19:39,150 --> 00:19:42,170
Winning a single US Senate seat was never the goal.
赢得一个美国参议院席位，从来不是最终目标。

206
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:46,050
The goal is to use that seat to transform our politics.
目标是利用这个席位，改变我们的政治。

207
00:19:47,971 --> 00:19:55,093
Because it is high past time that we get money out of politics, put money in your pocket,
因为我们早就应该让金钱退出政治，让人民的口袋充实起来，

208
00:19:55,103 --> 00:19:57,193
And pass Medicare for All.
通过全民医疗保险。

209
00:19:57,193 --> 00:20:02,450
The beauty and soul of America is that we the people are what America is all about.
美国的美与灵魂就在于：我们人民，才是美国的全部意义。

210
00:20:02,710 --> 00:20:05,090
We deserve an America for all her kids.
我们值得拥有一个属于所有孩子的美国。

211
00:20:05,570 --> 00:20:07,270
So Michigan, let's go build it.
所以密歇根，让我们一起去建设它。

212
00:20:07,430 --> 00:20:07,950
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。